<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Si Thep</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Si Thep is an ancient city in Phetchabun province in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, with a double moated town and monuments of the Dvaravati period and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> influence, from roughly the 6th to the 13th century. Its Buddhist and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> sculpture and brick monuments such as Khao Klang Nai are among the finest of the period. It was inscribed as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 2023.</p></div>
